        "title": "07 - Sealants and Caulks",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     SEALANT / CAULK LANDSCAPE                               │\n│                                                                             │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │  FIRST SPLIT: Static joints vs. Dynamic joints                      │   │\n│  │                                                                     │   │\n│  │  CAULK  ──── fills static gaps (trim to wall, no movement)         │   │\n│  │  SEALANT ─── accommodates movement (expansion joints, envelope)    │   │\n│  │                                                                     │   │\n│  │  \"Caulk\" and \"sealant\" are used interchangeably in trade           │   │\n│  │  but sealants have a rated movement accommodation factor (MAF)     │   │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                                             │\n│  SILICONE          POLYURETHANE        ACRYLIC LATEX       BUTYL RUBBER    │\n│  Most flexible     Paintable           Paintable           Tacky/roofing   │\n│  UV/temp extreme   Masonry/concrete    Interior trim       HVAC tape       │\n│  Not paintable     Horizontal joints   Lowest cost         Not paintable   │\n│  ±50% MAF          ±25% MAF            ±12.5% MAF          ±12.5% MAF     │\n│                                                                             │\n│  SMP HYBRIDS ─────── Silicone flexibility + polyurethane paintability      │\n│  INTUMESCENT ──────── Fire-rated through-penetrations                      │\n│  EPDM TAPE ────────── Pre-formed gaskets, roofing, windows                │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    }
